%% Payment State Machine Transition Sequence Diagram
%% Story #002: Implement Payment State Machine Service
%%
%% This diagram shows the sequence of operations when transitioning
%% a payment from one state to another using the PaymentStateMachine service.

sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as Client/Service
    participant PSM as PaymentStateMachine
    participant Validator as State Validator
    participant DB as PostgreSQL Database
    participant Events as payment_events Table

    Note over Client,Events: Payment State Transition Flow

    Client->>PSM: transition(paymentId, toState, metadata)
    activate PSM

    PSM->>PSM: Log debug: Attempting transition

    PSM->>DB: SELECT * FROM payments WHERE id = paymentId
    activate DB
    DB-->>PSM: Return payment object
    deactivate DB

    alt Payment not found
        PSM->>PSM: Log error: Payment not found
        PSM-->>Client: throw PaymentNotFoundError
    end

    PSM->>Validator: isTransitionAllowed(fromState, toState)
    activate Validator
    Validator->>Validator: Check ALLOWED_TRANSITIONS map
    Validator-->>PSM: Return boolean (allowed/denied)
    deactivate Validator

    alt Invalid transition
        PSM->>PSM: Log warn: Invalid transition
        PSM-->>Client: throw InvalidTransitionError
    end

    Note over PSM,Events: Atomic Database Transaction

    PSM->>DB: RPC: transition_payment_state(...)
    activate DB

    DB->>DB: BEGIN TRANSACTION
    DB->>DB: SELECT FOR UPDATE (row lock)

    alt State mismatch (race condition)
        DB-->>PSM: Return error: State mismatch
        PSM-->>Client: throw StateTransitionError
    end

    DB->>DB: UPDATE payments SET state = toState
    DB->>Events: INSERT INTO payment_events
    Events-->>DB: Return event_id
    DB->>DB: COMMIT TRANSACTION

    DB-->>PSM: Return success + event_id
    deactivate DB

    PSM->>DB: SELECT * FROM payments WHERE id = paymentId
    activate DB
    DB-->>PSM: Return updated payment
    deactivate DB

    PSM->>DB: SELECT * FROM payment_events WHERE id = event_id
    activate DB
    DB-->>PSM: Return payment event
    deactivate DB

    PSM->>PSM: Log info: Transition successful

    PSM-->>Client: Return TransitionResult (event + payment)
    deactivate PSM

    Note over Client,Events: Audit Trail Complete
